# Multi-LLM

Call the `multi_llm` tool with the argument text above, converted to its four
properties exactly as that tool's own argument descriptions specify. The tool is
the only supported entry point on this host: it appends the flags this host
requires, refuses the ones it owns, and supervises the run to a terminal result.
Do not reach the dispatcher any other way.

Read the result's `exit` and `next` the way the dispatcher's own contract reads
them. {NEEDS_HUMAN_RULE}

`user_next_step` is the phase after this one, for the user to type: never run it
yourself; end your report with its `markdown`, copied as it is (each command stays alone in its fenced block, each why and note stays plain text, the manual tasks it lists included). Say "Workflow complete." only when it is `complete`, never while it names a `command`: the workflow goes on. It is
never a tool call, unlike `next`, which is one.

When the result carries `validation_counts` (a review phase's does), report
them, and if `needs_human_decision` or `validation_failed` is non-zero point at
`report.md` for those groups; they are decided later, when the suggestions are
applied. A result without that key has no counts to report, so do not mention
them. When the result carries a `notice` (`result.notice`, a finished run's: what it left out or could not check, such as items it did not apply or that nothing ran this repository's tests), report what it says, every part of it, as plain text.
